{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat global_memory_summary.md; cat claims_grounding.json'","aggregated_output":"# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Overlap Aware Target Risk Benchmark Selection; status=idea_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=the cycle supplies a testable proposal but no evaluated finding that changes an evidence-backed recommendation.\n  - evidence: No recent ideas or attempts. Supplied accepted incumbent combined_score=0.9527030000575736, correct=true; its exact named program source path was unavailable. Public matrix structure supports covariance conditioning but no empirical improvement is established. Considered diversity-only selection, unsupported score-adaptive querying, and nonlinear completion; chose a small overlap-shrunk cross-target selector with fixed-target and held-out-family controls. No experiments were run. Only local memory target created or used: ideas/01_overlap_aware_target_risk_benchmark_selection/memory.md.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-07T05:58:37.284239+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: exit=1; cause unavailable; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Score Adaptive Latent Mixture Benchmark Design; status=idea_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=an unexplained execution failure and an untested alternative provide no evidence-backed change to a distilled recommendation.\n  - evidence: Read task/skill documents, supplied histories/manifests/memory/conclusions and prior candidate interface/source only. RPC supplies historical masks, normalized scores, availability and sequential observations; no family labels or outer fixed-target control. Prior exit=1, combined_score=null, correct=false has unknown cause and establishes neither scientific underperformance nor a particular protocol defect. Considered global covariance, one latent Gaussian and raw neighbor kernels; selected a masked latent Gaussian mixture for score-adaptive querying with K=1 and mean fallbacks. No new experiments, numerical probes, installation or task execution. Required JSON rubric arrays reviewed directly; each implementation rubric has executable source_contains patterns. Only local memory target created or used: ideas/02_score_adaptive_latent_mixture_benchmark_design/memory.md.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-07T06:09:49.663879+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: exit=1; cause unavailable; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Saturation Aware Monotone Skill Benchmark Design; status=idea_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=unexplained aggregate execution failures and an untested saturation hypothesis provide no evidence-backed change to distilled recommendations.\n  - evidence: Both recent attempts exited 1 with combined_score=null and correct=false; causes remain unknown. Prior candidate-interface/idea records expose normalized historical scores, masks, availability and sequential observations, not family labels or external fixed-target control. Considered global covariance, latent mixtures and neighbor transfer; selected a shrunk monotone scalar-skill model to test nonlinear saturation with nested task-mean and linear controls. No candidate/evaluator execution, numerical probe or literature lookup. Authored matching rubric arrays reviewed directly; implementation rubrics use 1–8 executable source_contains patterns. Only cycle-local memory target created or used: ideas/03_saturation_aware_monotone_skill_benchmark_design/memory.md.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-07T06:24:36.310628+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: exit=1; cause unavailable; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n{\n  \"scope\": \"Final evaluation results are independent of search selection. Implementation descriptions use the inspectable retained source, without claiming byte-identical final-snapshot identity.\",\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\"claim\": \"The final evaluation completed and qualified; qualification is not proof of broad generalization.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.qualification.status\", \"final.qualification.outcome\", \"final.qualification.correct\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The retained original reference has zero measured search score change; three alternative evaluations are unscored and do not establish measured losses or failure causes.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\", \"study.investigation_outcome\", \"study.search_score_delta\", \"study.attempts.total\", \"study.attempts.scored\", \"study.attempts.unscored\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The pooled studied score is 0.9527636891 and equivalent normalized MAE is 0.0472363109; rounded values in the abstract, results, and pooled table are 0.9528 and 0.0472.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Random-query low-rank pooled score is 0.9364101694, equivalent MAE 0.0635898306; the studied-minus-random difference is 0.0163535197.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\", \"final.metric.random_lowrank_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The supplied pooled paired family-clustered interval against random-query factors is [0.0148071678, 0.0184780194], not an interval against ridge or for subgroups.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\", \"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Information-selected ridge scores 0.9482262260 (MAE 0.0517737740), with descriptive studied-minus-ridge difference 0.0045374631 and no supplied paired significance interval.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.combined_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Medoid ridge scores 0.9327472830 (MAE 0.0672527170), mean offset 0.9206056682 (MAE 0.0793943318), and historical means 0.9068768878 (MAE 0.0931231122).\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.copy_score\", \"final.metric.constant_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The studied method has the highest pooled observed score among the six evaluated policies, without statistical superiority being established against all comparators.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\", \"final.metric.random_lowrank_score\", \"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.copy_score\", \"final.metric.constant_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Three final seeds are 1009, 1013, 1019; replay is excluded from primary means and figures.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#aggregation\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Figure 2, supplementary Table 2, and derived_results.json retain each of the twelve primary source/split/seed cells and six policies, using control=false and replay=false.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"build_paper_artifacts.py\", \"derived_results.json\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The studied policy has higher observed scores than random-query factors in all twelve retained primary cells and the highest three-seed mean in each of four source/split conditions.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"derived_results.json#conditions\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Studied condition means are 0.9496/0.9442 for MTEB model/family splits and 0.9591/0.9582 for Open LLM model/family splits, rounded from saved observations.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"derived_results.json#conditions\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Pooled source scores are 0.9468974985 for MTEB and 0.9586298797 for Open LLM; they do not constitute controlled source-difficulty comparisons.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.mteb_score\", \"final.metric.open_llm_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Open LLM family split at seed 1019 gives studied score 0.9531041725 versus information-selected ridge 0.9533160600, a retained local reversal.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[2].solution.cases\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Pooled independently deranged-history score is 0.9233917542 and actual-minus-control gap is 0.0293719349.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.permuted_score\", \"final.metric.corruption_gap\", \"final.metric.combined_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Every retained source/split/seed pair has a lower observed studied-policy score under historical-column derangement, as shown in Figure 3 and supplementary Table 3; the contrast changes learning, querying, and target composition jointly.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\", \"final.metric.corruption_gap\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#permute_training\", \"tables/controls.tex\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The final required cases completed and reset replay passed; these are interface/execution controls, not comprehensive validity guarantees.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.failed_episode_fraction\", \"final.metric.control_failure_fraction\", \"final.metric.reset_replay_ok\", \"final.qualification.status\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Supplementary Figure 4 shows only the studied-policy measured checkpoint arrays, increasing in each retained actual trajectory; no baseline checkpoint comparison, fixed-panel curve, or universally sufficient budget is inferred.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Recorded seed durations are 24.0816306723, 22.8890082091, 23.0760153015 seconds, excluding independent acquisition; no measured inference-cost, end-to-end storage, or speed advantage is asserted.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The inspectable retained source implements masked alternating ridge factors, fixed observed column means, and SVD initialization; lambda=0.1, candidate ranks 1/2/4/8, seeded 10% cell validation, at most four validation sweeps and eight refit sweeps capped by requested steps.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Hoerl\", \"Koren\", \"Jain\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L45-L83\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Equations 1 and 3 describe clipped remaining-target 1-MAE and context-independent ridge latent prediction; availability is known and historical missing cells are masked, not observed zeros.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#curve_score\", \"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L110-L142\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The retained-source acquisition in Equation 4 uses a unit-noise quadratic trace-reduction proxy, includes the queried coordinate, and ignores purchased score values. Equation 5 is a fixed-target matrix identity, not an MAE optimality theorem.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Chaloner\", \"Cohn\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#L114-L127\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Random LF uses matching reference factor fit/prediction construction; the ridge comparators use zero-filled centered covariance and penalties 0.01/0.1/1 chosen with every-fifth-row historical validation; means and mean-offset policies use random legal queries.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#reference_fit,predict_factors,run_baseline\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The readable retained and original reference files match, but exact byte-level identity to the separately hashed final snapshot is not independently certified; mechanism interpretation is conditional on supplied-source association.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\", \"source_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The evaluated source regimes are separately fitted MTEB embedding-model scores and Open LLM six raw generative benchmark columns; no learned cross-source transfer is asserted.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"MTEB\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/audit.json#sources,extraction\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#build_case\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Pinned MTEB revision is 6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383; pinned Open LLM revision is 9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2. MTEB extraction uses natural-bound original test scores and default/English task/revision/subset columns; Open LLM uses raw scores. The latter dataset license is undeclared.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"MTEB\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/audit.json#sources,extraction\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The inspected final protocol uses model and heuristic name-family disjoint groups, approximately 70% historical groups, twenty-observation MTEB column support, and coverage filters; family labels are not authoritative lineage.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#split_components,require_disjoint_rows,build_case\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/audit.json#extraction\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"MTEB checkpoints are 1/2/4/8, Open LLM checkpoints 1/2/3. Target, row, checkpoint, seed, split, source weighting is nested and equal at each level; control/replay have zero primary weight.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#aggregation,production\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The supplied interval uses 200 paired family-clustered bootstrap draws with RNG24681357 and 2.5/97.5 percentile endpoints, shared family multiplicities across paired policies, cases and seeds within source. It is preserved, not reconstructed from seed means.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\", \"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Efron\", \"Owen\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#uncertainty\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Documented evaluation versions are CPython3.12.15, NumPy1.26.4, SciPy1.12.0, PyArrow16.1.0, with CPU operation, isolation and broker requirements; this is not a newly measured cross-platform reproduction.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#runtime\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#RPC\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"No fixed untouched target panel, response-adaptive selector, controlled nonlinear superiority, universal budget sufficiency, or family-held-out tuning is supported. Diagnostic descriptions remain unverified.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.attempts.unscored\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#limitations\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"MMLU, MTEB and HELM motivate heterogeneous evaluation coverage; item-level compression in tinyBenchmarks and metabench differs from buying aggregated benchmark scores; BenchBench motivates care about agreement methodology.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.allowed.MMLU\", \"ref.allowed.MTEB\", \"ref.allowed.HELM\", \"ref.allowed.Tiny\", \"ref.allowed.Metabench\", \"ref.allowed.BenchBench\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"MMLU\", \"MTEB\", \"HELM\", \"Tiny\", \"Metabench\", \"BenchBench\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Observational scaling laws and Sloth motivate low-dimensional multi-benchmark capability descriptions, without establishing interpreted skill recovery or scaling-law estimation by this study.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.allowed.Observational\", \"ref.allowed.Sloth\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Observational\", \"Sloth\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Matrix factorization, probabilistic/Bayesian factor models, and implicit-feedback models provide distinct methodological precedents; this study fits regularized numerical-score coordinates rather than a fully Bayesian or implicit-preference model.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.allowed.Koren\", \"ref.allowed.PMF\", \"ref.allowed.BayesianMF\", \"ref.allowed.Hu\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Koren\", \"PMF\", \"BayesianMF\", \"Hu\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Convex, spectral, and alternating matrix completion methods have assumption-dependent guarantees that are not verified for the selectively observed matrices here.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.allowed.CandesRecht\", \"ref.allowed.CandesTao\", \"ref.allowed.Keshavan\", \"ref.allowed.Mazumder\", \"ref.allowed.Jain\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"CandesRecht\", \"CandesTao\", \"Keshavan\", \"Mazumder\", \"Jain\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Ridge regularization, Bayesian design and statistical active learning are methodological context for the inspected solves and proxy, not evidence of novel architecture or universal MAE optimality.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.allowed.Hoerl\", \"ref.allowed.Chaloner\", \"ref.allowed.Cohn\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Hoerl\", \"Chaloner\", \"Cohn\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Missing-data assumptions and incomplete-data likelihood methods are separate from merely optimizing a masked loss; generic bootstrap and dependent-array resampling motivate specifying the resampling unit.\", \"source_ids\": [\"ref.allowed.Rubin\", \"ref.allowed.Schafer\", \"ref.allowed.Dempster\", \"ref.allowed.Efron\", \"ref.allowed.Owen\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Rubin\", \"Schafer\", \"Dempster\", \"Efron\", \"Owen\"]}\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
